Chapter: SourceDefWireGuard
  cites Foreword chapter SourceDefWire
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The record's ninth field is a length, and it is read off the disk. Every arm
 below is one hostile value of it against a line that is 12 characters long
 after the ninth pipe.

 Arms 1 to 3 are the shapes a WELL-FORMED record produces and a guard must not
 refuse: the ordinary case, content running exactly to the end, and the empty
 content whose offset is one past the last character. Arms 4 to 7 are hostile.
 4 and 5 kill the guest outright without the bound (measured 2026-08-16:
 substring answers !EXC=06 both for a length past the end and for a negative
 one), and 6 is the same kill wearing different clothes -- text-to-integer
 answers 1511 for "abc" rather than failing, so a corrupt length field arrives
 as a plausible large number rather than as a zero.

 We say:

Section: Reading the answer

  show-decode : Maybe SourceDefWire -> Text
  show-decode (m) =
    when m
     is None -> "refused"
     is Just (w) -> "[" & w.sdw-content & "]"

  show-fields : Maybe SourceDefWire -> Text
  show-fields (m) =
    when m
     is None -> "refused"
     is Just (w) -> w.sdw-hash & "/" & w.sdw-author & "/" & show (w.sdw-timestamp)

Section: The lines

 Nine pipes, then the content. Only the ninth field and the content differ
 between arms.

  line-ok : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|12|demo content"
  line-short : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|4|demo content"
  line-empty : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|0|"
  line-over : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|99|demo content"
  line-negative : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|-5|demo content"
  line-garbage : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|abc|demo content"
  line-nopipe : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77"

 ARM 9 IS THE ONE THAT GOT PAST THE FIRST BOUND. The guard was written as
 `p9 + 1 + clen > text-length line`, which is defeated by the value an attacker
 chooses: text-to-integer answers 9223372036854775807 for this field, the sum
 wraps negative, the comparison is false and the record is admitted. Run
 against that guard on 2026-08-16 the guest died `!EXC=06`. A ceiling that the
 attacker can reach around is not a ceiling, which is why the check subtracts
 now, and why arms 4 and 5 alone could not have caught this.

  line-overflow : Text = "abc123|p/q|Quire|Chap|||val|77|9223372036854775807|demo content"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("1 ok=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-ok))
    print-line-uni ("2 short=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-short))
    print-line-uni ("3 empty=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-empty))
    print-line-uni ("4 over=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-over))
    print-line-uni ("5 negative=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-negative))
    print-line-uni ("6 garbage=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-garbage))
    print-line-uni ("7 nopipe=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-nopipe))
    print-line-uni ("8 fields-survive=" & show-fields (sdw-decode line-ok))
    print-line-uni ("9 overflow=" & show-decode (sdw-decode line-overflow))
  end
